      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1915-04-17_WidnesExaminer_art0018" n="art0018">
        <head>FOR YOUR</head>
        <p>FOR YOUR</p>
        <p>POULTRY AND CHICK FEED CLOVER MEAL, FISH MEAL.</p>
        <p>CARTER &amp; SON, L.". BRIDGE ST., WARRINGTON.</p>
        <p>Corn, Flour and Provender</p>
        <p>Stores.</p>
        <p>CORN raiLLERs.</p>
        <p>WRITE Orpington Stock Cockerels for Sale, Martin Burnham, Esq., Pedigree Stock, 10/6; 12/6 each.—Mr. B. J. Parsonage, Willow Bank Farm, Whitley, Northwich.</p>
        <p>REALLY %RELIABLE EGGS for Hatching from most hardy birds. ALL GUARANTRED FERTILE, and sold at most reasonable price. WHITE LEGHORNS, from Tom Barron's best 286 egg pen, bought last autumn. Bar- ron's price, a guinea; mine, ss. per dozen. WHITE WYANDOTTES. Selected layers, mated with Tom Barron's 286 egg strain 1914 Cockerel; 4s. dozen. BLACK MINORCAS. Abbot's and Cook's well-known laying strain. They are positive wonders. Quite as good winter layers as any heavier breed. Never broody. Very large eggs. 4s. dozen. BUFF ORPINGTON'S. Magnificent hens, Abbot's and Cook's laving strain, mated to huge prize 1914 Cockerel. Positive machines for winter eggs, when eggs mean money. 4s. dozen. Reduction for large quantities. ' PURE AYLESBURY DUCKS, from selected layers, which begin laying in January and ensure early market for ducklings. Massive birds. making up to 141 b. 3s. Gd. dozen. Apnly in good time. as I have many customers.--RECTOR, Stave- ley Rectory, Knaretborough. ,‘;</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1915-04-17_WidnesExaminer_art0019" n="art0019">
