        <p>ELECTRIC LIGHT FOR STOCKTON HEATH. Parish Council Withdraw Opposition To Corporation's Order. CONCESSIONS TO THE SUBURBANS An inquiry was held at the Board of Trade Offices. on Tuesday with reference_ to the Elec- tric Lighting Extension Order sought by the Warrington Corporation to enable them to run their mains to and supply Stockton Heath with electricity. The Corporation and the Rural District Council were represented at the inquiry. We understand that prior to the inquiry a meeting took place at the Town Hall between the representatives of the Stockton Heath Parish Council and the Corporation. . The Parish Council had announced their intention of opposing the application for the Order from the Board of Trade, .but the conference re- sulted in terms of settlement being arranged. We are informed that the Corporation now undertake to lay mains in Walton-road, Grap- penhall-road, a portion of Whitefield-road and London-road, to the south of. Victoria-square, within a limited period of time. Further, we learn that satisfactory arrangements were made with regard to a future supply of electric light in Ellesmere-road and Fairfield-road. In view of the agreement arrived at during the conference the Parish ..council. decided to withdraw .their opposition to the Corporation's application .for the Order. NEW RECRUITING AGENTS.. - The following have been,added to the list of recruiting agents in the -40th Recruiting Area, which embraces Warrington and district:— Borough of Warrington, Mr. T. •H. Spinks, Town Clerk's Office ; Eccleston Parish, Mr. C. H. Taylor.</p>
